From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] VideoOutput: the stereo layer is active only once the
 compositor took its declaration; a failed declaration withdraws the layer,
 says why, and the video is drawn the ordinary way

The layer attached and committed the two views even when stereo_declare_wayland failed (only a qCWarning), and stereoLayerActive (layerWanted &&
presenterReady) never looked at the declaration: the person saw the packed frame, both views side by side in each eye, while the player said 3D
(ORDER 49's October picture).

The surface is now declared when the layer is made, before any buffer is attached to it (the same single declaration, no longer in the commit of the
first frame), and a refusal is kept for the layer's life. A layer whose declaration failed attaches and commits nothing on any of its three routes
(window surface, own DMA-BUF buffers, wl_shm), and its presenter is not valid and says why: VideoOutput does not use it, stereoLayerActive is false,
the item draws the video through the scene graph (one view, by stereoView), and the new property stereoLayerFailure holds the reason (also logged
once, qt.multimedia.video.stereolayer). The reason stays while the same 3D video plays, so the declaration is not asked for again at every frame,
and clears when the 3D video ends or the item changes window: the next 3D video declares again.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/multimediaquick/qquickvideostereolayer.cpp
+++ b/src/multimediaquick/qquickvideostereolayer.cpp
@@ -892,6 +892,7 @@
     wp_color_management_surface_v1 *colorSurface = nullptr;
     Buffer buffers[3];
     bool declared = false;
+    int declareError = 0; // errno of the declaration the compositor library refused: kept for the layer's life, nothing is shown without the declaration
     bool stereoInitialized = false;
     QRect rect;
     QRect placed;
@@ -907,11 +908,32 @@
     BufferFormat gpuWanted = BufferFormat::Xrgb8888;
 
     void place();
+    bool ensureDeclared();
     bool presentDmabuf(const QQuickVideoDepth::LayerSource &source, bool swapEyes, const QRect &crop, BufferFormat format, BufferFormat *used,
                        QString *why, bool *backpressure);
     void dispatch() { wl_display_dispatch_queue_pending(display, queue); }
 };
 
+// The surface is declared as full side by side stereo content once, before anything is attached to it: a buffer of two views is never committed
+// to a surface the compositor has not taken as stereo content (it would show the packed frame, flat). A refusal stays: the layer is withdrawn
+// (declarationFailure()) and the caller draws the video the ordinary way.
+bool QQuickVideoStereoLayer::Private::ensureDeclared()
+{
+    if (declared)
+        return true;
+    if (declareError)
+        return false;
+    const int result = stereo_declare_wayland(surface, STEREO_SBS_FULL, STEREO_CLASS_VIDEO, STEREO_VIDEO_CURRENT);
+    if (result < 0) {
+        declareError = -result;
+        qCWarning(qLcStereoLayer) << "declaring the stereo content failed:" << strerror(declareError)
+                                  << "- the layer is not used, the video is drawn the ordinary way, not in 3D";
+        return false;
+    }
+    declared = true;
+    return true;
+}
+
 // The views drawn into buffers the layer allocated (GBM), given to the compositor as DMA-BUF; false with the reason in *why, or with
 // *backpressure when the compositor holds every buffer
